    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><fw place="top-left" type="adressline">Mc Millan Co<lb/>60 Fifth
                            Avenue<lb/><rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York
                            City</rs></fw>
                    <dateline><date when="1946-07-23">July 23,
                        1946</date></dateline><salute>Gentlemen:</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>I have received the enclosed letter (translated by myself) from the niece of <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__1438" type="person">Prof. Rudolf Otto</rs>, Miss
                        <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3526" type="person">Gretel Ottmer</rs>, 16
                    Kaiser St. <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__306" type="place"
                    >München</rs><!-- <q>Muenchen</q> -->, 13 b, <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__122"
                        type="place">Germany</rs>. The letter is <sic>selfexplanatory</sic>. I would
                    be very grateful to you if you would either answer me or directly <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__3526" type="person">Miss Ottmer</rs> about the
                    questions indicated in <rs ref="#L10955" type="letter">her letter</rs>.</p>
                <p>I was a <sic>collegue</sic> of <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1438" type="person"
                        >Prof. Otto</rs> in <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__279" type="place"
                        >Marburg</rs>, <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__122" type="place">Germany</rs>,
                    for two years.</p>
                <closer><salute>Yours sincerely</salute><signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928"
                            type="person">Paul Tillich</rs>
                        <lb/>Professor at Union Theological Seminary.</signed><pb n="2"/></closer>

                <postscript>
                    <fw place="top-middle" type="heading"><hi rend="u">TRANSLATION</hi></fw>
                    <p><!-- <q>......</q> -->... Would you be able to approach McMillan, 60 Fifth
                        Avenue, <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York City</rs>?
                        They have published <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1438" type="person">Rudolf
                            Otto</rs>&apos;s <rs ref="tillich__67N7XVQF" type="work">EASTERN AND
                            WESTERN MYSTICISM</rs>. As <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__2759"
                            type="person">my mother</rs> passed away in 1942 I am the only member of
                        the family alive. I know that we are not permitted to handle any business
                        affairs, but I would like to know whether there are any chances for years to
                        come. <rs ref="tillich__67N7XVQF" type="work">The book</rs> is out of print
                        over here and we do not know when a new print will be possible. I feel that
                            <rs ref="tillich__67N7XVQF" type="work">Dr. Otto&apos;s. work</rs>
                        should be made available to theologians.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
